# Scaffold Planning Task

## Goal

Decide the project boundaries that should exist before an agent generates backend, frontend, feature, or validation code.

Use this task as a planning checklist. It is not a request to copy framework configuration before the selected stack exists.

The planning output should distribute durable guidance to the right place: product intent in the main spec, layer direction in the architecture spec, repeatable procedures in task docs, and mechanical rules in scripts when the target stack exists.

## Checklist

1. Confirm the selected stack and directories:
   - backend: `{% if backend_stack == 'none' %}not selected yet{% elif backend_stack == 'rust' %}Rust workspace under crates/{% else %}.NET solution at {{ dotnet_solution_path }}{% endif %}`
   - frontend: `{% if frontend_stack == 'none' %}not selected yet{% else %}{{ frontend_stack }} app under {{ frontend_dir }}{% endif %}`
2. Update `docs/specs/{{ main_spec_slug }}-v0.1.md` with the current product scope, user journeys, and data/contract ownership.
3. Update `docs/specs/architecture-layering-v0.1.md` before creating code that crosses a new layer boundary.
4. Define the dependency direction for each feature. Code should depend forward through the documented layers and must not reverse-import runtime/UI concerns into lower layers.
5. Pick exactly one DTO/source-of-truth strategy before the frontend consumes backend data:
   - generated OpenAPI and generated frontend types,
   - shared schema package,
   - tRPC or another typed RPC boundary,
   - GraphQL schema plus code generation.
6. Add or plan a freshness check for the chosen contract strategy. If the backend/frontend do not exist yet, record the intended check and add it when the stack is scaffolded.
7. Use 700 lines as the default maintainability threshold for hand-written product source files. Extract a cohesive domain, layer, route, component, or helper before growing past it, then list any stack-specific exceptions.
{% if backend_stack == 'rust' %}
   - Exception: organize Rust modules by domain rather than line count.
{% endif -%}
{% if frontend_stack != 'none' -%}
8. Explicitly evaluate Playwright for this frontend. If stable browser journeys exist or are part of the immediate scaffold, install Playwright, wire `test:e2e`, and tag specs with `@impact-*`; otherwise record why E2E is deferred and what condition will make it active. Do not wire browser E2E into `finalize.sh` until the frontend can start reliably and at least one stable user journey exists.
{% endif %}
## Example Output

This is an example shape, not a required architecture. Replace names and layers with what the project actually needs.

```text
Feature: Saved Searches

Backend:
  Domain/SearchQuery          owns validated query value objects.
  Application/SavedSearches   owns use cases and repository/provider traits.
  Infrastructure/SearchStore  implements persistence.
  Api/SavedSearchEndpoints    maps HTTP requests/responses and OpenAPI metadata.

Frontend:
  features/saved-searches/types.ts       imports generated API types and defines local view types only.
  features/saved-searches/config.ts      owns labels, limits, and filter modes.
  features/saved-searches/repo.ts        calls shared/api and translates transport errors.
  features/saved-searches/service.ts     owns pure view transformations and business rules.
  features/saved-searches/runtime.ts     owns loading/error state, effects, and orchestration.
  features/saved-searches/components/    renders UI and emits user events.

Direction:
  DTO source of truth -> repo -> service -> runtime -> components/pages.
  Components do not call fetch. Runtime does not import components. Service does not import runtime.

Checks:
  Active now: default 700-line product source threshold with documented exceptions, plus frontend fetch/import layering checks.
  Deferred: Playwright journey for create/edit/delete after routes and seeded test data exist.
```

## Output

Record:

- layer map or feature folder shape.
- DTO/source-of-truth choice and check command.
- checks that are active now.
- checks intentionally deferred until the stack exists.
- open questions that block scaffolding.
